            <ArticleTitle>[From surgical pain to pain surgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>151-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>From the historical viewpoint, a change of attitude towards pain and the possibilities opened up by general anesthesia from 1846 onwards were needed to bring about the advent of a surgery specialized in the cure of pain. The individual stages in this development, up to Leriche's &quot;Chirurgie de la douleur&quot;, are illustrated by reference to the relevant sources.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
